            "description": "",
            "summary": "(Reuters) -Shares of FrontView REIT fell 3.9% in their debut on the New York Stock Exchange on Wednesday, valuing the commercial real estate investment trust at $487.9 million.  It sold 13.2 million shares in the IPO, raising $250.8 million.  With the U.S. Federal Reserve joining major economies in cutting interest rates, analysts expect REITs to be among the prime beneficiaries, as lower rates make financing real estate deals easier.",
